(function(Q,k,r,n){Q.route[k]=r;var o="",p=0;n.forEach(function(x){o+=r.slice(p,x[0])+x[1];p=x[0]});Q.routenh[k]=o+r.slice(p)})(window.MNM_QUICK,"11-15","<div class=\"sc-wrap\"><p class=\"sc-pick\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> No start city picked: choose one in the <b>Start</b> box in the top bar to see its route for levels 11–15.</p><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"ailvorith\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Ail&#x27;Vorith · levels 11–15 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 11–15: Goblins, spirits, House quest Part 2 begins</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Camps (wiki levels): spirits and elementals 9-11 (a torn spirit, a wandering soul, a forsaken soul, rogue/stray/swift elementals), a failed experiment 10-11, Deepgulp warrior/scavenger/hunter 10-11, Deepgulp berserker/mystic 12-13, a floating skull 13-15. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith (rev 83176, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Named: Gloweye 10-11 (Deepgulp goblin camp), The Discarded 10+ (lighthouse: Uneven Mantle, Shroomwood Staff, Rough-Forged Leggings), Bubbles 10+ (oozes by the deep gnome researchers: Charming Talisman, Cave Mitts), Cook Deepbite 14-15 (back of the Deepgulp caves: Crude Gatorhide Cap). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith (rev 83176, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Cook_Deepbite\">Wiki: Cook Deepbite</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Deepgulp kills raise Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith and Ail&#x27;vorith Exiles (and lower Clan Deepgulp). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Citizens_of_Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki faction: Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27vorith_Exiles\">Wiki faction: Ail&#x27;vorith Exiles</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Cook_Deepbite\">Wiki: Cook Deepbite</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor monk\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor, Monk only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> At 13: Klavel Sul sends you to Miniel Ubast in the Shol&#x27;tar for Xal&#x27;tharn Part 2 (needs the city access from Part 1). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-xal\"><summary><b>House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest)</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl Part 1: 8+, Part 2: 13+</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Your class House quest: chest armor at 8, city access, House Xal&#x27;tharn faction and the Iron Render weapon.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Klavel Sul</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Foreign Quarter, Military Outpost: the building on the left past the bridge and gate, back of the room with the melee trainers (the quest page calls it the Obsidian Academy; see the Monk trainer note)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>Part 1: 8+, Part 2: 13+</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Inquisitor, Monk</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>Obsidian Shackle from the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest. Deep Common language.</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Part 1 grants city access (wiki). Part 2 turn-in: &#x27;You gain faction with House Xal&#x27;tharn&#x27;. Other faction hits are marked as unknown on the wiki: no sourced data yet.</td></tr></table><h5>Steps <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h5><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Part 1 (8+): hail Klavel Sul; say &#x27;The Queen&#x27;, then &#x27;I would be a cenobite&#x27;, then &#x27;Do you have a task for me?&#x27;. You receive the Remnant Satchel (6 slots).</li><li>Swim around the west of the city, where elementals and skulls patrol the west island shores. Kill a separated skull and a spectral remnant (both 8-11) for 6 Lost Skull.</li><li>Combine the satchel and hand it to Klavel Sul (XP). Say &#x27;I swear allegiance to the Queen!&#x27; (XP). Inquisitors receive the Dull Iron Cuirass; Monks the Simple Chestwrap.</li><li>Part 2 (13+): before 13, Klavel says you lack the skill. At 13, hail him and say &#x27;I accept.&#x27; He gives a summons for Lady Miniel in the Shol&#x27;tar, beneath the Queen&#x27;s arena: take the road on the right into the Dark City and go through the dungeon gates near the bank.</li><li>Give the summons to Miniel Ubast in the Inquisitor&#x27;s Guildhall (NPC page: enter the main city, turn right, up the ramp, the prison guarded by Inquisitors, up one floor and through the door). Ask about the duty and where the exiles are.</li><li>Go to the exile camps to the south, by the river into the Great Cavern Sea: past the waterfall where snakes gather, on the bottom floor past the invisible hired thug. Kill exiles until you have one each of the Unknown, Silver and Gold Sigil of a Lesser House (unique: one of each).</li><li>Keep killing the bottom-floor exiles until Gullach Otal&#x27;qar (16-17, named Fighter) spawns in their place, then kill him for Gullach&#x27;s Head.</li><li>Hand the 3 sigils and the head to Miniel Ubast.</li></ol><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Lost Skull x6</b>: a separated skull (8-11, Enchanter: Mesmerize, Silence), a spectral remnant (8-11, Fighter), west island shores</li><li><b>Sigil of a Lesser House (Unknown, Silver, Gold)</b>: exiles: a starving outcast, a runaway, a praying exile (exile mobs are 15-22)</li><li><b>Gullach&#x27;s Head</b>: Gullach Otal&#x27;qar (16-17), bottom floor of the exile area behind the hired thug</li></ul><p><b>Turn in:</b> Part 1: Klavel Sul. Part 2: Miniel Ubast (Shol&#x27;tar, inside the city)</p><p><b>Rewards:</b> XP: XP at both Part 1 turn-ins and at the Part 2 turn-in · Item: Inquisitor: Dull Iron Cuirass (chest AC 9, STA +1, INT +1, HP +5) and Iron Render (1H slash 7/30, STR +2, STA +1, INT +1, HP +5, Mana +5). Monk: Simple Chestwrap and Tarnished Iron Bo. · Coin: none listed · Faction: City access (Part 1); House Xal&#x27;tharn + (Part 2)</p><p><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Reward conflict resolved, Cuirass wins. The quest page listed a Xal&#x27;tharn Pendant from its first version (2026-09-23, beta 0.30.0.0) until rev 78132 (2026-10-07, after the 0.30.2.1 release patch), when an editor replaced it with the Dull Iron Cuirass for Inquisitors. That editor created the Dull Iron Cuirass item page with full stats four minutes later. The Pendant item page was last touched 2026-09-26, and the Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests summary page that still says Pendant was never updated. The newer first-hand edit with an item page wins over the older summary. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/w/index.php?title=House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)&amp;action=history\">Wiki edit history: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Dull_Iron_Cuirass\">Wiki: Dull Iron Cuirass (item page created 2026-10-07)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Xal%27tharn_Pendant\">Wiki: Xal&#x27;tharn Pendant (item page, last edited 2026-09-26)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span></p><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> Whether Monks (or pre-release characters) still get the Pendant as well: no sourced data yet. No talk page exists for the quest. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Xal%27tharn_Pendant\">Wiki: Xal&#x27;tharn Pendant (item page, last edited 2026-09-26)</a></span></p><p><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Do Part 2 at about 15-17, not 13: the sigil exiles are 15-22 and Gullach is 16-17 (wiki levels). Bring a group or a healer. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith (rev 83176, 2026-10-18)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-house-xaltharn-quest\">quest helper</a> · <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/House_Xal%27tharn_(Quest)\">Wiki: House Xal&#x27;tharn (Quest) (rev 82660, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Klavel_Sul\">Wiki: Klavel Sul (rev 82871, 2026-10-17)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Miniel_Ubast\">Wiki: Miniel Ubast</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Sigil_of_a_Lesser_House_(Gold)\">Wiki: Sigil of a Lesser House (Gold)</a></span></p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger archer fighter\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger, Archer, Fighter only</span> <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Stolen Gems (min level 10, Archer/Ranger/Fighter): goblin camp gems for a class weapon. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ail%27Vorith_Class_Quests\">Wiki: Ail&#x27;Vorith Class Quests</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-gems\"><summary><b>Stolen Gems</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 10</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Class weapon (Legion Recurve or Legion Longsword) from goblin camp gems.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Glaeron Kes&#x27;tel</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Ail&#x27;Vorith</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>10</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Ranger</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive Legion Recurve (Fighters quest reward is the Legion Longsword ) from Glaeron Kes&#x27;tel.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>This quest starts at the conclusion of the Ail&#x27;Vorith Starter Quest after you receive your Obsidian Shackle.</li><li>Laren Drin&#x27;dar is located in the Foreign Quarter of Ail&#x27;Vorith.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Lvl 14+</b></li><li>Glaeron Kes&#x27;tel is located House Vael&#x27;xirith in Ail&#x27;Vorith.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Go and slaughter goblins in their camps until you find all four: Pilfered Topaz, Pilfered Ruby, Pilfered Sapphire, Pilfered Emerald. Give these to Glaeron.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Legion Recurve (Fighters quest reward is the Legion Longsword ) from Glaeron Kes&#x27;tel.</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Stolen_Gems\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-stolen-gems\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-13</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Blind Midden: 10-13 mobs on the top floor, named at 12 (Underboss Vekrizin, Cedrius the Cutter, Blacksmith Jerictus, Wikket Two-Wands, Reviver Vlarek, Mother Gummer). Basement named start at 15. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Blind_Midden\">Wiki: Blind Midden (rev 83212)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-ailvorith-merit\"><summary><b>Mark of Merit</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1 (repeatable)</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> XP and Marks of Merit for the Midden Mark Menu while you clear Blind Midden named mobs.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Receptionist Naleth&#x27;ra</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Blind Midden ground floor (map point 1)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1 (repeatable)</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>None listed.</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><h5>Steps <span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span></h5><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Kill any named mob in Blind Midden and loot its corpse item (no drop).</li><li>Turn the corpse in to Receptionist Naleth&#x27;ra.</li></ol><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Corpse of &lt;named&gt;</b>: any Blind Midden named (top floor named are 7-12, basement named 15+)</li></ul><p><b>Turn in:</b> Receptionist Naleth&#x27;ra</p><p><b>Rewards:</b> XP: Experience · Item: Blind Midden Mark of Merit (Midden Mark Menu rewards are random) · Coin: none listed · Faction: no sourced data yet</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Mark_of_Merit\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-mark-of-merit\">quest helper</a> · <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Mark_of_Merit\">Wiki: Mark of Merit</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Blind_Midden\">Wiki: Blind Midden (rev 83212)</a></span></p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Great Cavern Sea camp levels (wiki zone page rev 83098; mob pages): by the Ail&#x27;Vorith zoneline a shore beetle 15, a shelter bat 16, a shallows basilisk 17 (the Survey targets); goblin island 19-23; Wasp and Beetle Island 22-26; Basilisk Island 27-28; Spider Cave 29-30. Per-camp mobs are listed in the level bands below. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Great_Cavern_Sea\">Wiki: Great Cavern Sea (rev 83098, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/A_shore_beetle\">Wiki: a shore beetle (15)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/A_shelter_bat\">Wiki: a shelter bat (16)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/A_shallows_basilisk\">Wiki: a shallows basilisk (17)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> Great Cavern Sea, Blacktide Orc Cove: orcs 11-17 (a Blacktide hauler, hull hauler and lookout 11-14?, a cargo guard 15-17?, Morgak Foamscar 15-17?). The question marks are the zone page&#x27;s own (rev 83098) and the orc mob pages list no level, so treat these as estimates. Morgak&#x27;s page adds one FACT: he dropped Blacktide Chain Leggings (AC 13, STR +2, STA +2). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Great_Cavern_Sea\">Wiki: Great Cavern Sea (rev 83098, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/A_Blacktide_hauler\">Wiki: a Blacktide hauler (rev 74514, no level listed)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/A_Blacktide_lookout\">Wiki: a Blacktide lookout (rev 74513, no level listed)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Morgak_Foamscar\">Wiki: Morgak Foamscar (rev 83094, 2026-10-18)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Danger: Vhaleth Hal&#x27;kareth, a level 60 Deep Elf Wizard, stands near the wizard pyramid in the Great Cavern Sea. His mob page says he casts a greater fireball for 1280. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Great_Cavern_Sea\">Wiki: Great Cavern Sea (rev 83098, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Vhaleth_Hal%27kareth\">Wiki: Vhaleth Hal&#x27;kareth (rev 73852, 2026-09-24)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Keep well away from the wizard pyramid at every level on this route: nothing else in the zone is above 30. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Great_Cavern_Sea\">Wiki: Great Cavern Sea (rev 83098, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Vhaleth_Hal%27kareth\">Wiki: Vhaleth Hal&#x27;kareth (rev 73852, 2026-09-24)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Great Cavern Sea, player-tracked: hunting levels 16-24, most at 17; coin per kill 8cp-2sp 25cp, average 87cp (361 kills). This is the best measured range for the zone as a whole, not per camp. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.wiki/zones/great-cavern-sea\">monstersandmemories.wiki: Great Cavern Sea (player-tracked levels and coin)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step sc-fr\" data-scr=\"deep-elf\"><span class=\"sc-who\">Deep Elf only</span> <span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> Surface option: wererats outside the Underdocks (wiki 10-12) were used for Night Harbor faction (forum). Do not kill Deepcut bandits: they lower Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith (wiki). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://forum.monstersandmemories.com/d/1616-deep-elf-non-kos-night-harbor\">Forum: Deep Elf Non-KOS Night Harbor (2026-10-04)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Underdocks\">Wiki: Underdocks</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Citizens_of_Ail%27Vorith\">Wiki faction: Citizens of Ail&#x27;Vorith</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Lurithos Kest): L11 Exposing Shot; L12 Barbed Arrow II, Caltrops; L13 Oil Trap I; L14 Sniper&#x27;s Blind; L15 Quick Shot II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L11 Unifying Anthem; L12 Chords of Quickness, Faedawyn&#x27;s Arcane Alacrity, Overture of Speed, Siren&#x27;s Allure; L13 Frightful Screech; L14 Selstie&#x27;s Aeolian Aria; L15 Whistling Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L12 Bestial Glimpse, Invigorate Companion, Patch Companion; L15 Savage Strike II. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Zalethra Drezzorith): L12 Blessed Barrier II, Disease Protection, Healing light, Lesser Pacify, Prayer of the Faithful II, Smite the Dead II, Stun, Summon Drink. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L12 Charm Beasts, Dispel Magic, Enduring Breath, Fear Beasts, Jackal Form, Lesser Frostbite, Mantle of Autumn, Mantle of Spring, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Spark of Earth, Wolf Form. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Lothur Varros): L12 Charm the Elements, Companion Strike III, Elemental Flash III, Fear the Elements, Fire Protection, Lesser Elemental Fury, Lesser Elemental Spellshield, Lull the Elements, Minor Creation: Air, Restrain the Elements, Summon Companion, Summon Heavy Cloth Bandage, Summon Minor Wind Blade. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Amarah Ith&#x27;vayen): L12 Captivate, Charm, Enchant Bronze Bar, Enduring Breath, Fascinate, Fracture Magic, Illusion: Gnome, Incinerate Mana, Lesser Vertigo, Lull, Mind Surge, Summon Companion, Torment III. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Tharkan Inathar): L11 Cross Cut; L12 Kneebreaker, Shield Block I; L13 Frenzy I; L14 Disarm; L15 Juggernaut, Second Wind. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Nurvol Cereveth): L11 Invisibility; L12 Aura of Rapidity, Mana Ward, Memory Fog, See Invisibility; L13 Lesser Spellshield; L14 Psychic Choke; L15 Purge. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Klavel Sul): L11 Celestial Strike II; L12 Wind Style; L14 Flying Kick. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Vaslir Naiyth): L12 Command the Dead, Dark Embrace, Leech Lifeforce, Locate Corpse, Mana Surge, Restrain the Dead, Spirit Splinter, Summon Companion, Summon Zombie, Surging Shadows, Transfer Strength. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Mentvar Drezzorith): L11 Disease Protection; L12 Hallowed Ground, Repel the Dead, Vengeful Smite; L14 Aura of Piety, Snare the Dead; L15 Unleash the Light. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Laren Drin&#x27;dar): L11 Opening Strike II, Poison Protection; L12 Barbed Shield, Finishing Blow II, Lesser Healing Poultice, Maiming Shot; L13 Sneak; L14 Apex Predator, Hunter&#x27;s Recovery, Leading Shot II, Minor Pack Recovery; L15 Camouflage, Longstrider Stance, Salvage Arrows. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Zorvanna Velgarrith): L12 Vial of Smoke; L13 Pick Pocket; L14 Rain of Steel I; L15 Blinding Powder. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Vhalrek Velgarrith): L12 Feign Death (Spell); L13 Fear; L14 Sacrifice Minion. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L12 Consume, Consuming Pact, Cure Disease, Dispel Magic, Enduring Breath, Omen of Enfeeblement, Root. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Ilnara Hal&#x27;kareth): L11 Lesser Spellshield; L12 Arcane Spear II, Kinetic Ward II; L14 Seclusion. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Vhasilla Hal&#x27;kareth): L12 Bind Vision, Eldritch Ward II, Lesser Flash of Ice, Minor Burst of Magic, Purge. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"faelindral\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Faelindral · levels 11–15 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 11–15: Calafreyan ruins, Mezzatrian spiders, Sporehaven, Blacktide Bay</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Calafreyan ruins (south of Scout Amberward, over two bridges): Calafreyan soldiers and archers 11-13, an Elven Field Sergeant ~12, a fallen elven champion ~13. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Archer_Starter_Quest_(Faelindral)\">Wiki: Archer Starter Quest (Faelindral) (rev 75499)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Mezzatrian broodlings and scions (10-12) on the platform across the broken bridge (across the fallen log, up the ramp, behind the waterfall, follow the bridges). A River Elemental (11-12) is in the pond by the Newbie Lift. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Druid_Starter_Quest_(Faelindral)\">Wiki: Druid Starter Quest (Faelindral) (rev 80229)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Sporehaven Karst myconids (~13-15), aggressive at night. Taeresh Deathcharmer (13?) is in the Orc Cave. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Evershade_Weald\">Wiki: Evershade Weald (rev 83151, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Shaman_Starter_Quest_(Faelindral)\">Wiki: Shaman Starter Quest (Faelindral) (rev 79993)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-faelindral-menace\"><summary><b>Mushroom Menace</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl &lt;= 5 (mobs to kill much higher: yellow to L12)</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Staff of Spores plus Circle of Spores faction (Naelira&#x27;s Court −). The wiki gives the minimum level as 5 or lower, but the mobs are up to about 12.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Sporeweaver Underveil</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Evershade Weald · Sporeweaver Underveil, Sporehaven Karst (the mushroom cave near Faelindral)</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>&lt;= 5 (mobs to kill much higher: yellow to L12)</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Circle of Spores (+); Naelira&#x27;s Court (-)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>Staff of Spores; (exp)</td></tr></table><h5>Mobs and items</h5><ul class=\"tight\"><li><b>Prismatic Gills</b>: a beguiled bluecap (~13-15), at night</li><li><b>Enchanted Water x4</b>: a beguiled water elemental in the naiad cave upstream</li></ul><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Sporeweaver Underveil is located in the mushroom cave close to Faelindral.</li><li>Collect Prismatic Gills from a beguiled bluecap during the night and deliver them to Sporeweaver Underveil.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Need item verification along with quantity required for turn-in.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Circle of Spores (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Naelira&#x27;s Court (-)</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Underveil&#x27;s Phial from Sporeweaver Underveil.</li><li>Collect 4 Enchanted Water from a beguiled water elemental in the naiad cave upstream and combine them in Underveil&#x27;s Phial.</li><li>After handing Sporeweaver Underveil the completed sample you receive Staff of Spores.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Staff of Spores from Sporeweaver Underveil.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Need combined item name, along with relevant dialogue, exp, money, faction hits.</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Mushroom_Menace\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-mushroom-menace\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-09-27</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Blacktide Bay (wiki 10-30): gloom widows 9-11, undead gnomish engineers, surveyors and architects 11-13, a net weaver 12, Gurowl the Beast, a Fellstone ritualist and Frimbus Darplefen 14, Commander Rursk 15. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Blacktide_Bay\">Wiki: Blacktide Bay</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.wiki/zones/blacktide-bay\">monstersandmemories.wiki: Blacktide Bay (player-tracked levels and coin)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Keeper&#x27;s Bight spider log: deadwood recluses 11-14. A Reddit player levelling at 13 near Evershade Weald was pointed there. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Keeper%27s_Bight\">Wiki: Keeper&#x27;s Bight</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://www.reddit.com/r/MonstersAndMemories/comments/1vkskp0/levelling_location_near_evershade_weald_level_13/\">Reddit: Levelling location near Evershade Weald level 13 (2026-08-10)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Keeper&#x27;s Bight docks: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-faelindral-hale\"><summary><b>Hale&#x27;s Haul</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> 20 silver plus Langsdorfian League, Red Mantles and Village of Penshaw faction for five sunken crates. Great bight sharks (20-30, aggressive) patrol the bay.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Captain Hale</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Keeper&#x27;s Bight · Captain Hale, the last ship on the Keeper&#x27;s Bight docks</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Langsdorfian League (+); Red Mantles (+); Village of Penshaw (+)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); (money:0,0,20,0)</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>On the docks of Keeper&#x27;s Bight, in the last ship, you&#x27;ll find Captain Hale.</li><li>Captain Hale has asked for your assistance recovering five lost crates of goods from the bottom of the bay beneath the dock, which were lost in a recent storm.</li><li>The Salvaged Cargo Crate are resting on the bottom of the ocean. These are collected using MUD commands.</li><li>Additionally, the crates have a cooldown before they can be looted by another player. You will need to use the MUD /look command to confirm if a crate is lootable before attempting to pick it up.</li><li>Be mindful, as there are several a great bight shark swimming around the bay, which are level 20-30 and aggressive.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: If the crate cannot be looted...</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: If the crate can be looted...</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Salvaged Cargo Crate.</li><li>Once you have 5 crates, return to Captain Hale.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive 20 silver from Captain Hale.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Langsdorfian League (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Red Mantles (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Village of Penshaw (+)</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Hale%27s_Haul\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-hales-haul\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-09-30</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Keyaryn Thornshade): L11 Exposing Shot; L12 Barbed Arrow II, Caltrops; L13 Oil Trap I; L14 Sniper&#x27;s Blind; L15 Quick Shot II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Pine Brightreed (starter); Sylphrena Starfall and Laenyth Windharp): L11 Unifying Anthem; L12 Chords of Quickness, Faedawyn&#x27;s Arcane Alacrity, Overture of Speed, Siren&#x27;s Allure; L13 Frightful Screech; L14 Selstie&#x27;s Aeolian Aria; L15 Whistling Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Relgen Greenblade, then Aerin Mossfang): L12 Bestial Glimpse, Invigorate Companion, Patch Companion; L15 Savage Strike II. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L12 Blessed Barrier II, Disease Protection, Healing light, Lesser Pacify, Prayer of the Faithful II, Smite the Dead II, Stun, Summon Drink. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (High Gatekeeper Sylvarya Starveil): L12 Charm Beasts, Dispel Magic, Enduring Breath, Fear Beasts, Jackal Form, Lesser Frostbite, Mantle of Autumn, Mantle of Spring, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Spark of Earth, Wolf Form. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L12 Charm the Elements, Companion Strike III, Elemental Flash III, Fear the Elements, Fire Protection, Lesser Elemental Fury, Lesser Elemental Spellshield, Lull the Elements, Minor Creation: Air, Restrain the Elements, Summon Companion, Summon Heavy Cloth Bandage, Summon Minor Wind Blade. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L12 Captivate, Charm, Enchant Bronze Bar, Enduring Breath, Fascinate, Fracture Magic, Illusion: Gnome, Incinerate Mana, Lesser Vertigo, Lull, Mind Surge, Summon Companion, Torment III. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Vaelric Ironbark, then Craftguard Vinebrow): L11 Cross Cut; L12 Kneebreaker, Shield Block I; L13 Frenzy I; L14 Disarm; L15 Juggernaut, Second Wind. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L11 Invisibility; L12 Aura of Rapidity, Mana Ward, Memory Fog, See Invisibility; L13 Lesser Spellshield; L14 Psychic Choke; L15 Purge. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L11 Celestial Strike II; L12 Wind Style; L14 Flying Kick. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L12 Command the Dead, Dark Embrace, Leech Lifeforce, Locate Corpse, Mana Surge, Restrain the Dead, Spirit Splinter, Summon Companion, Summon Zombie, Surging Shadows, Transfer Strength. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L11 Disease Protection; L12 Hallowed Ground, Repel the Dead, Vengeful Smite; L14 Aura of Piety, Snare the Dead; L15 Unleash the Light. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Captain Relgen Greenblade): L11 Opening Strike II, Poison Protection; L12 Barbed Shield, Finishing Blow II, Lesser Healing Poultice, Maiming Shot; L13 Sneak; L14 Apex Predator, Hunter&#x27;s Recovery, Leading Shot II, Minor Pack Recovery; L15 Camouflage, Longstrider Stance, Salvage Arrows. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Elyndiir Nightshade): L12 Vial of Smoke; L13 Pick Pocket; L14 Rain of Steel I; L15 Blinding Powder. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L12 Feign Death (Spell); L13 Fear; L14 Sacrifice Minion. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Varilis Thornvine): L12 Consume, Consuming Pact, Cure Disease, Dispel Magic, Enduring Breath, Omen of Enfeeblement, Root. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L11 Lesser Spellshield; L12 Arcane Spear II, Kinetic Ward II; L14 Seclusion. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L12 Bind Vision, Eldritch Ward II, Lesser Flash of Ice, Minor Burst of Magic, Purge. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"night-harbor\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Night Harbor · levels 11–15 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 11–15: Crypt by day and night, Tel Ekir Ashira, docks goblins</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Night Harbor docks goblins, west of the twilight harbor by the cranes: no faction hit, but social. Hunting guide: solo 13-15, group 8-12. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Night Harbor crypt by day: diseased bats and catacombs rats (10), dusty scarabs (11), cracked beetles (12), hardened scarabs (13), diseased beetles (14). Named: a sanguine bat 12, a pristine beetle 13, an old scarab 14, an ornate beetle 15. The beetles and scarabs raise Red Mantles. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Night_Harbor\">Wiki: Night Harbor (rev 83168, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Red_Mantles\">Wiki faction: Red Mantles</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Cemetery key (opens the crypt at night): <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-key\"><summary><b>Night Harbor Cemetery Key Quest</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> The key opens the cemetery at night (skeletons 12-16 and named). Part 1 uses crypt rats and bats (10).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Gatekeeper Nusder</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Night Harbor · Gatekeeper Nusder at the Red Mantle Keep entrance to the cemetery</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>(exp); Key to the Night Harbor Cemetery</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 1 - Prove Your Worth</b></li><li>Gatekeeper Nusder is located at the Red Mantle Keep entrance to the cemetery in Night Harbor.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Gatekeeper Nusder may be referring to player level as &#x27;proof of worth&#x27; here.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Need to verify - minimum starting level for quest.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Empty Satchel from Gatekeeper Nusder.</li><li>The gates to the cemetery will close at sunset and re-open at sunrise. NPCs inside the cemetery become aggressive and higher level once the sun sets.</li><li>Enter the gate and kill a diseased bat or a catacombs rat and loot Chunk of Diseased Meat x10. The meat is NODROP and not guaranteed on every kill, so plan accordingly if grouping here.</li><li>After combining the meats in the Empty Satchel, you receive Fetid Satchel.</li><li>Give the Fetid Satchel to Gatekeeper Nusder.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: No exp or faction hits for this step.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 2 - The Source of Corruption</b></li><li>Find Liyna Esueiruc in the second floor (teleporter puts you on floor 3) of the Night Harbor library (which is due east from Gatekeeper Nusder, at the Spellbinders of the Spire).</li><li>Give Liyna Esueiruc the Fetid Satchel.</li><li>Give Liyna Esueiruc the Fetid Satchel again.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Lightly Scented Piece of Parchment from Liyna Esueiruc.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: No faction or exp</li><li>Return to Gatekeeper Nusder and hand him the Lightly Scented Piece of Parchment.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: No faction</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 3 - A Sign of Necromancy</b></li><li>You are to head back into the cemetery and find a Bloodied Engraved Rune.</li><li>Kill a pristine beetle, a sanguine bat, an old scarab, an ornate beetle, or other named that requires camping till it spawns at the top of the cemetery and loot Bloodied Engraved Rune.</li><li>Return to Gatekeeper Nusder and give him Bloodied Engraved Rune along with Lightly Scented Piece of Parchment.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Simple Piece of Parchment from Gatekeeper Nusder.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Part 4 - Further Research</b></li><li>Return to Liyna Esueiruc and give her Bloodied Engraved Rune along with Simple Piece of Parchment.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Any faction hits?</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Scented Piece of Parchment from Liyna Esueiruc.</li><li>Return to Gatekeeper Nusder and hand him the Scented Piece of Parchment.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Key to the Night Harbor Cemetery from Gatekeeper Nusder.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: To be continued, probably requires killing a noble skeleton, a bejeweled skeleton, a majestic skeleton or a crowned skeleton.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: More details are required...</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Night_Harbor_Cemetery_Key_Quest\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-night-harbor-cemetery-key-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-12</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Crypt by night (needs the key): skeletons 12-15 (decrepit, risen, stumbling, cackling) with named noble 13, bejeweled 14, majestic 15 and crowned 16; skeletal priests 18-19 and Malchiok the Priest 25-26. Hunting guide: solo 12?, group 10-14?. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Night_Harbor\">Wiki: Night Harbor (rev 83168, 2026-10-18)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Tel Ekir, Ashira entrance: younglings 9-11, skinners 10-11, oracles and wanderers ~12-14, alphas ~14, and named Roa the Huntress 12, Ayip and Yapala 13, Hadhraman 17. The alpha camp is higher. Hunting guide: group 9-16. Player-tracked: most at 13. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Tel_Ekir\">Wiki: Tel Ekir</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.wiki/zones/tel-ekir\">monstersandmemories.wiki: Tel Ekir (player-tracked levels and coin)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Tel Ekir named bounty: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-ayip\"><summary><b>Wanted: Ayip &amp; Yapala</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl ?</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Red Mantles faction and The Impaler for two Tel Ekir named (13).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Guard Atep</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Night Harbor</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>?</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Wanted:_Ayip_&amp;_Yapala\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-wanted-ayip-yapala\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-04-12</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Sungreet Strand beach, past the Ashira camps: thugs, acolytes and skintakers (~11-14). Damage is high, so bring a tank and a healer. Hunting guide: solo 12?, group 8-12. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Sungreet_Strand\">Wiki: Sungreet Strand</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Infested Crypt, larger spiders 12-14 and a frenzied crypt guardian (~12). The crypt broodmother is 16. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Infested_Crypt\">Wiki: Infested Crypt</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Next armor set: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-cinder\"><summary><b>Cinder Beetle Armor Quests</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-rec\">Recommended</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> The armor set after scarab. The Night Harbor page lists it at 14. Cinder workers (16-18) in the Sungreet quarry drop the parts (hunting guide).</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Hult Beetlewrangler</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Night Harbor · Hult Beetlewrangler, Sojourner Camp</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>Archer, Bard, Beastmaster, Cleric, Druid, Fighter, Inquisitor, Monk, Paladin, Ranger, Rogue, Shadow Knight, Shaman, Spellblade</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Cinder Beetle Shield</b></li><li>1x Cinder Beetle Legs</li><li>1x Cinder Beetle Carapace</li><li>Give Hult Beetlewrangler 1x Cinder Beetle Carapace and 1x Cinder Beetle Legs</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Cinder Beetle Boots</b></li><li>2x Cinder Beetle Legs</li><li>1x Cinder Beetle Carapace</li><li>Give a master blacksmith 1x Cinder Beetle Carapace and 2x Cinder Beetle Legs</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Cinder Beetle Helm</b></li><li>2x Cinder Beetle Carapace</li><li>2x Cinder Beetle Legs</li><li>2x Charcoal</li><li>1x Copper Dagger</li><li>1x Cinder Beetle Mandible</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Cinder Beetle Greaves</b></li><li>1x Cinder Beetle Gland</li><li>1x Cinder Beetle Blood</li><li>3x Cinder Beetle Carapace</li><li>2x Cinder Beetle Legs</li><li>1x Cinder Beetle Serrated Mandible</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Cinder Beetle Breastplate</b></li><li>2x Resin</li><li>2x Cinder Beetle Blood</li><li>1x Crude Fish Oil</li><li>1x Twilight Bay Rum</li><li>4x Cinder Beetle Carapace</li><li>2x Cinder Beetle Serrated Mandible</li><li>1x Giant Cinder Beetle Eye</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Cinder_Beetle_Armor_Quests\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-cinder-beetle-armor-quests\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-13</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional, the Bends: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-gang\"><summary><b>Riverbend Gang Wars Quest</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 10</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Bends Garrison faction, at the cost of the Ten Hooks and Waterdogs gangs.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Corporal Theodora</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Night Harbor</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>10</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Your faction standing with Bends Garrison got better.</li><li>Your faction standing with Cult of the Living City got better. &quot; 1 full blue &quot;</li><li>Your faction standing with Ten Hooks got worse. &quot; 1 full blue &quot;</li><li>Your faction standing with Waterdogs got worse. &quot; 1 full blue &quot;</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li></ol><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Riverbend_Gang_Wars_Quest\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-riverbend-gang-wars-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-11</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional faction: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-heads\"><summary><b>Ashira Infiltrator Heads</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl ~15</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> Red Mantles faction, but it costs Citizens of Night Harbor if you over-kill Mayana and Jumthem.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Red Mantle Quartermaster</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Night Harbor</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>~15</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>Red Mantles (+); Langsdorfian League (+); Seafarers Consortium (-)</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>You receive Hidden Ashira&#x27;s Head from Red Mantle Quartermaster.</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>After completing The Yowling, it is discovered that certain residents of Night Harbor are more than what they appear.</li><li>Slaying these residents in disguise will yield Hidden Ashira&#x27;s Head that may be turned in to the Red Mantle Quartermaster for faction with the Red Mantles.</li><li>This quest is repeatable, but caution is advised. Slaying Mayana and Jumthem too many times will cause significant faction loss with the City of Night Harbor and the Pyrmos Mercenaries.</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: It is not known whether there are more disguised ashira NPCs within Night Harbor. More information is required...</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Missing dialogue here? How does the player know to turn the head in to the quartermaster?</li><li>Hand in either Mayana&#x27;s Head or Jumthem&#x27;s Head to the Red Mantle Quartermaster.</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Hidden Ashira&#x27;s Head from Red Mantle Quartermaster.</li><li>Hand in Hidden Ashira&#x27;s Head to the Red Mantle Quartermaster.</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Red Mantles (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Langsdorfian League (+)</li><li class=\"dim\">Faction: Seafarers Consortium (-)</li><li class=\"dim\">Note: Are these faction hits correct?</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Starts after The Yowling. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span></p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Ashira_Infiltrator_Heads\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-ashira-infiltrator-heads\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-01</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Optional, Shaded Dunes: <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a href=\"/quest-helper.html\">Wiki quest walkthroughs (quest helper)</a></span><details class=\"sc-q\" id=\"scq-night-harbor-chompers\"><summary><b>Chompers&#x27; Hide Tunic Quest</b> <span class=\"sc-tag sc-opt\">Optional</span> <span class=\"dim\">lvl 1</span></summary><p class=\"sc-why\"><span class=\"badge strat\">strategy</span> A tunic from Chompers (16), a crocodile that spawns randomly on the Shaded Dunes beach.</p><table class=\"kv sc-kv\"><tr><th>Giver</th><td>Cheikho</td></tr><tr><th>Where</th><td>Shaded Dunes</td></tr><tr><th>Level</th><td>1</td></tr><tr><th>Classes</th><td>any</td></tr><tr><th>Needs first</th><td>none listed</td></tr><tr><th>Faction</th><td>no sourced data yet</td></tr><tr><th>Turn in</th><td>see the steps below (wiki walkthrough)</td></tr><tr><th>Rewards</th><td>Chompers Hide Tunic</td></tr></table><ol class=\"tight sc-steps\"><li>Cheikho is at the hunters camp on the eastern side of the large, rocky mound separating the smuggler area from the oasis with the ghouls. You can see the camp from the beach.</li><li>Chompers is a level 16 crocodile which will spawn randomly along the beach.</li><li>Kill Chompers and loot Chomper&#x27;s Hide.</li><li>Return to Cheikho and give him 1 x Chomper&#x27;s Hide.</li><li class=\"dim\">Experience</li><li class=\"dim\">Receive: You receive Chompers Hide Tunic Chompers&#x27; Hide Tunic from Cheikho.</li><li class=\"sc-qh\"><b>Related Quests</b></li><li>Spectral Armor Quest</li></ol><p><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The wiki marks this quest page as needing more info; missing steps: no sourced data yet.</p><p class=\"sc-ql\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Chompers%27_Hide_Tunic_Quest\">wiki</a> · <a href=\"/quest-helper.html#q-chompers-hide-tunic-quest\">quest helper</a> · wiki walkthrough updated 2026-10-07</p></details></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Jacobin Yeats): L11 Exposing Shot; L12 Barbed Arrow II, Caltrops; L13 Oil Trap I; L14 Sniper&#x27;s Blind; L15 Quick Shot II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Jamee Langris): L11 Unifying Anthem; L12 Chords of Quickness, Faedawyn&#x27;s Arcane Alacrity, Overture of Speed, Siren&#x27;s Allure; L13 Frightful Screech; L14 Selstie&#x27;s Aeolian Aria; L15 Whistling Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Leila Ghasem): L12 Bestial Glimpse, Invigorate Companion, Patch Companion; L15 Savage Strike II. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Dalinder Grammanoot): L12 Blessed Barrier II, Disease Protection, Healing light, Lesser Pacify, Prayer of the Faithful II, Smite the Dead II, Stun, Summon Drink. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Rolan Talmula): L12 Charm Beasts, Dispel Magic, Enduring Breath, Fear Beasts, Jackal Form, Lesser Frostbite, Mantle of Autumn, Mantle of Spring, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Spark of Earth, Wolf Form. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Tenebrim Tam): L12 Charm the Elements, Companion Strike III, Elemental Flash III, Fear the Elements, Fire Protection, Lesser Elemental Fury, Lesser Elemental Spellshield, Lull the Elements, Minor Creation: Air, Restrain the Elements, Summon Companion, Summon Heavy Cloth Bandage, Summon Minor Wind Blade. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Master Wincog): L12 Captivate, Charm, Enchant Bronze Bar, Enduring Breath, Fascinate, Fracture Magic, Illusion: Gnome, Incinerate Mana, Lesser Vertigo, Lull, Mind Surge, Summon Companion, Torment III. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Fedamius Steele III): L11 Cross Cut; L12 Kneebreaker, Shield Block I; L13 Frenzy I; L14 Disarm; L15 Juggernaut, Second Wind. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Petra Gyle): L11 Invisibility; L12 Aura of Rapidity, Mana Ward, Memory Fog, See Invisibility; L13 Lesser Spellshield; L14 Psychic Choke; L15 Purge. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Chahaya Tam): L11 Celestial Strike II; L12 Wind Style; L14 Flying Kick. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Marvion Hallows, then Sekhmet): L12 Command the Dead, Dark Embrace, Leech Lifeforce, Locate Corpse, Mana Surge, Restrain the Dead, Spirit Splinter, Summon Companion, Summon Zombie, Surging Shadows, Transfer Strength. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Trey Fulton): L11 Disease Protection; L12 Hallowed Ground, Repel the Dead, Vengeful Smite; L14 Aura of Piety, Snare the Dead; L15 Unleash the Light. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Foss Dunestrider): L11 Opening Strike II, Poison Protection; L12 Barbed Shield, Finishing Blow II, Lesser Healing Poultice, Maiming Shot; L13 Sneak; L14 Apex Predator, Hunter&#x27;s Recovery, Leading Shot II, Minor Pack Recovery; L15 Camouflage, Longstrider Stance, Salvage Arrows. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Sinastin Aspenleaf): L12 Vial of Smoke; L13 Pick Pocket; L14 Rain of Steel I; L15 Blinding Powder. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Exavius Deathwhisper): L12 Feign Death (Spell); L13 Fear; L14 Sacrifice Minion. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Errol Shrewtender): L12 Consume, Consuming Pact, Cure Disease, Dispel Magic, Enduring Breath, Omen of Enfeeblement, Root. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Njau Hansou): L11 Lesser Spellshield; L12 Arcane Spear II, Kinetic Ward II; L14 Seclusion. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Olvin Viscus): L12 Bind Vision, Eldritch Ward II, Lesser Flash of Ice, Minor Burst of Magic, Purge. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul></div><div class=\"sc-route\" data-sc=\"underdocks\"><h3 class=\"sc-h\">Start-city route: Underdocks · levels 11–15 <span class=\"badge fact\">sourced route</span></h3><h4 class=\"sc-bh\">Levels 11–15: Elder shadowbones, Sporefather, Riddrick, Night Harbor docks</h4><ul class=\"sc-steps-list\"><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Elder shadowbones (10-12) and wererats (10-12); named the Sporefather (13-14, Ironroot Fists), Riddrick the Cursed (14, Riddrick&#x27;s Head for Ratkiller), Jumbe (14) and Munk (14). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Underdocks\">Wiki: Underdocks (rev 82552, 2026-10-17)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> storiesofmnm lists a mindless blightspore (Myconid, level 13) in a small cave in the northeast cavern of the Underdocks, tied to the Shaman starter quest and dropping a Blightspore Brain. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://storiesofmnm.com/wiki/npc/mindless-blightspore/\">storiesofmnm: Mindless blightspore</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Deepcut camps and the mine (group 10-16). Jorlach the Fearless near the entrance drops Jorlach&#x27;s Head, used in the Shadow Knight starter quest. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Deepcut_Bandits\">Wiki faction: Deepcut Bandits</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Underdocks\">Wiki: Underdocks (rev 82552, 2026-10-17)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Up in Night Harbor: the docks goblins by the cranes (no faction hit, solo 13-15, group 8-12), the Tel Ekir Ashira entrance (group 9-16), and the crypt by day (beetles and scarabs 10-15). <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Per-Level_Hunting_Guide\">Wiki: Per-Level Hunting Guide (rev 73595, 2026-09-22; marked work in progress)</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Night_Harbor\">Wiki: Night Harbor</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-step\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> Caves of Irem (wiki 13+; player-tracked 13-37, most at 13), north along the river from the Underdocks. <span class=\"sc-src\">Source: <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.miraheze.org/wiki/Caves_of_Irem\">Wiki: Caves of Irem</a>, <a class=\"ext\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\" href=\"https://monstersandmemories.wiki/zones/caves-of-irem\">monstersandmemories.wiki: Caves of Irem (player-tracked levels and coin)</a></span></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"archer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Archer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Simrut the Green (after Marshal Harding)): L11 Exposing Shot; L12 Barbed Arrow II, Caltrops; L13 Oil Trap I; L14 Sniper&#x27;s Blind; L15 Quick Shot II. <a href=\"/classref/archer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"bard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Bard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Crescindy (sells Bard songs)): L11 Unifying Anthem; L12 Chords of Quickness, Faedawyn&#x27;s Arcane Alacrity, Overture of Speed, Siren&#x27;s Allure; L13 Frightful Screech; L14 Selstie&#x27;s Aeolian Aria; L15 Whistling Slash II. <a href=\"/classref/bard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"beastmaster\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Beastmaster spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Gunder Dinnig (after Marshal Harding)): L12 Bestial Glimpse, Invigorate Companion, Patch Companion; L15 Savage Strike II. <a href=\"/classref/beastmaster/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"cleric\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Cleric spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Sister Marwen (trainer); Soren Akedd starts the quest): L12 Blessed Barrier II, Disease Protection, Healing light, Lesser Pacify, Prayer of the Faithful II, Smite the Dead II, Stun, Summon Drink. <a href=\"/classref/cleric/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"druid\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Druid spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Luskmit): L12 Charm Beasts, Dispel Magic, Enduring Breath, Fear Beasts, Jackal Form, Lesser Frostbite, Mantle of Autumn, Mantle of Spring, Minor Communion of Regeneration, Minor Regeneration, Spark of Earth, Wolf Form. <a href=\"/classref/druid/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"elementalist\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Elementalist spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Maude Astarace (after Marshal Harding)): L12 Charm the Elements, Companion Strike III, Elemental Flash III, Fear the Elements, Fire Protection, Lesser Elemental Fury, Lesser Elemental Spellshield, Lull the Elements, Minor Creation: Air, Restrain the Elements, Summon Companion, Summon Heavy Cloth Bandage, Summon Minor Wind Blade. <a href=\"/classref/elementalist/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"enchanter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Enchanter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Maude Astarace (after Marshal Harding)): L12 Captivate, Charm, Enchant Bronze Bar, Enduring Breath, Fascinate, Fracture Magic, Illusion: Gnome, Incinerate Mana, Lesser Vertigo, Lull, Mind Surge, Summon Companion, Torment III. <a href=\"/classref/enchanter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"fighter\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Fighter spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Gunder Dinnig (after Marshal Harding)): L11 Cross Cut; L12 Kneebreaker, Shield Block I; L13 Frenzy I; L14 Disarm; L15 Juggernaut, Second Wind. <a href=\"/classref/fighter/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"inquisitor\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Inquisitor spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L11 Invisibility; L12 Aura of Rapidity, Mana Ward, Memory Fog, See Invisibility; L13 Lesser Spellshield; L14 Psychic Choke; L15 Purge. <a href=\"/classref/inquisitor/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"monk\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Monk spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L11 Celestial Strike II; L12 Wind Style; L14 Flying Kick. <a href=\"/classref/monk/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"necromancer\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Necromancer spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Soren Akedd (starter quest)): L12 Command the Dead, Dark Embrace, Leech Lifeforce, Locate Corpse, Mana Surge, Restrain the Dead, Spirit Splinter, Summon Companion, Summon Zombie, Surging Shadows, Transfer Strength. <a href=\"/classref/necromancer/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"paladin\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Paladin spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L11 Disease Protection; L12 Hallowed Ground, Repel the Dead, Vengeful Smite; L14 Aura of Piety, Snare the Dead; L15 Unleash the Light. <a href=\"/classref/paladin/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"ranger\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Ranger spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Simrut the Green (after Marshal Harding)): L11 Opening Strike II, Poison Protection; L12 Barbed Shield, Finishing Blow II, Lesser Healing Poultice, Maiming Shot; L13 Sneak; L14 Apex Predator, Hunter&#x27;s Recovery, Leading Shot II, Minor Pack Recovery; L15 Camouflage, Longstrider Stance, Salvage Arrows. <a href=\"/classref/ranger/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"rogue\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Rogue spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Slylara Llumare): L12 Vial of Smoke; L13 Pick Pocket; L14 Rain of Steel I; L15 Blinding Powder. <a href=\"/classref/rogue/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shadow-knight\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shadow Knight spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Father Fyod (after Soren Akedd)): L12 Feign Death (Spell); L13 Fear; L14 Sacrifice Minion. <a href=\"/classref/shadow-knight/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"shaman\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Shaman spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Picci Manifold): L12 Consume, Consuming Pact, Cure Disease, Dispel Magic, Enduring Breath, Omen of Enfeeblement, Root. <a href=\"/shaman/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"spellblade\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Spellblade spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (your class trainer): L11 Lesser Spellshield; L12 Arcane Spear II, Kinetic Ward II; L14 Seclusion. <a href=\"/classref/spellblade/spells.html\">Full list</a></li><li class=\"sc-fc\" data-scc=\"wizard\"><span class=\"badge fact\">fact</span> <span class=\"sc-who\">Wizard spells</span> Buy or train each as you reach its level (Maude Astarace (after Marshal Harding)): L12 Bind Vision, Eldritch Ward II, Lesser Flash of Ice, Minor Burst of Magic, Purge. <a href=\"/classref/wizard/spells.html\">Full list</a></li></ul></div></div>",[[26092,"<p class=\"sc-nhnote\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The class notes below were written for a <b>Night Harbor</b> start (Night Harbor gates, the Night Market forge, Night Harbor camps). You picked Ail&#x27;Vorith: use the route above for where to go.</p>"],[41800,"<p class=\"sc-nhnote\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The class notes below were written for a <b>Night Harbor</b> start (Night Harbor gates, the Night Market forge, Night Harbor camps). You picked Faelindral: use the route above for where to go.</p>"],[77277,"<p class=\"sc-nhnote\"><span class=\"badge unc\">unverified</span> The class notes below were written for a <b>Night Harbor</b> start (Night Harbor gates, the Night Market forge, Night Harbor camps). You picked Underdocks: use the route above for where to go.</p>"]]);